<!--Post: 5808--><!--Time: 1107387957-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5808"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lmuncy316<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lmuncy316<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 02, 2005 - 3:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->We keep making comparisons of BTK &amp; the Zodiac, but what about the Son of Sam? BTK did make mention of Son of Sam in one of his letters.  And, BTK did say that he was from California and that he was needing a car to get to New York! BTK also has an infatuation with the number 3.  Three years after the Otero murders police receive their first letter from Son of Sam.  Compare the letter from Son of Sam to BTK&#39;s letters... the broken speech patterns... the references... the misspellings.  It was almost as if the Son of Sam was copycatting BTK&#39;s style of writing.  Now, I&#39;m not saying the Son of Sam is connected with BTK, but isn&#39;t it coincidental?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5808-->
<!--Post: 5814--><!--Time: 1107390472-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5814"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 02, 2005 - 4:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->There were theories prior to David Berkiwitz&#39;s arrest that these killings were the work of more than one person. It turned out Berkowitz was the Son of Sam but he may not have acted alone. <BR> <BR>His neighbor was Sam Carr who had a dog named Harvey that gave Berkowitz messages to kill according to Berkiwitz&#39;s mental defense. <BR>Sam Carr also had two sons John and Michael who were supposedly invloved in a Satanic cult and were friends of Berkowitz. Niether was arrested as an accomplice however one of them closely resembled a composite sketch provided by a witness. Both were dead within two years of Berkowitz&#39;s arrest. John of a supposed self-inflicted rifle shot to the face in Montana and Michael in a drunk driving accident in New York. <BR>Berkowitz implicated two other neighbors known as the Joker and the Duke of Death. They supposedly fled the area and were never questioned or identified. <BR>Berkowitz&#39;s mailman Andrew Dupay committed suicide within a year saying he was being threatened for things he knew. What things no one knows but he also the mailman for the Carrs as well. <BR>The Church of Final Judgement operated in the area and was supposedly a Satanic cult church that may have been involved in narcotics and child pornography. Berkowitz, the Joker, the Duke of Death and the Carr brothers may have been involved with this organization. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5814-->
<!--Post: 5868--><!--Time: 1107430228-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5868"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Openeyes<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Openeyes<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 3:30 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Have done alot of research on the cult theorey, out of everything Ive read on the boards this makes the most sense to me. It is errie that there were so many famous serial killers in the late 60&#39;s through the 70&#39;s and most of them have mentioned something about california, New york and even South dakota<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5868-->
<!--Post: 6270--><!--Time: 1107644917-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6270"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 3:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I was reading these posts today and recalled something coincidential included in the Son of Sam letters Berkowitz wrote.  <BR>&#34;Here are some names to help you along. Forward them to the Inspector for use by the NCIC&#40;nation crime information center&#41;. They have everything on computer, everything. They just might turn up, from some other crimes. Mabye they can make associations.&#34; <BR>&#34;Duke of Death, Wicked King Wicker, The Twenty-two Disiples of Hell, And Lastley, John Wheaties, rapist and suffocator of young girls.&#34; <BR> <BR>The Wheaties reference is what intrigues me. Why did Tom recently have that note to BTK, about eating his Wheaties. <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6270-->
<!--Post: 6455--><!--Time: 1107803752-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6455"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bodycheck<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bodycheck<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 07, 2005 - 11:15 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->man...my SOS lore is out of date... <BR>but i thought id add a couple thoughts... <BR> <BR>Openeyes, John who&#39;s cult ties are documented and traced to Dakotas &#40;cant remember if it was north or south&#41; is the infamous &#34;John Wheaties&#34; Berkowitz refers to... <BR> <BR>Also if i remember correctly...there was a LOT of evidence tying the Carrs to the murders as possible controllers or manipulators of Berkowitz... <BR> <BR>The amount of death that followed around the key figures in that case surely points to more than just lil ol David...especially since he was locked up when the rest of the characters started turning up dead.. <BR> <BR> <BR>B <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6455-->
